## Living Incantation

A living incantation is a length of metal strut from the elevator shaft of the [[Geography/Færrin/Infinite Horizon/Far Realms/Hesperid|Hesperid]], patterned over into the ship's six-fold shape and cursed into life. They climb out of the skulls lining the shaft, red light glowing in the sockets as they come, and they walk on wall and ceiling as readily as on the floor. They are angry at whoever has entered the shaft.

Their metal turns a blade and blunts a bullet. They do not bleed, no poison or sickness touches them, and no spell of the mind finds anything to hold. Harm spread wide, a burst or a song that catches several at once, hurts them where a single good blow does not, and they come apart under it. They cannot fly, and they cannot pass the doorway out of the shaft, though they can reach whoever stands at its lip. The shaft holds more of them than any fight will clear; they come out of the walls as readily as out of the skulls.

## Walking Figure

A tall, shiny metal figure walks the snows of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] without sinking, standing about eight feet. A faint green light, like a tethered ghost, drifts at its head, leaving it and returning. It seems to have no weakness, and it notices what passes it only slowly; it held still as a statue on a rack at a [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]] safe house before it walked.
